(332269, 25496, 8953, '<td valign="top">nice image 8</td>', 'nice image 8', '2003-06-20 03:24:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(332285, 25440, 4967, '<td valign="top">The thumb looks pitch black, the photo looks fricking awesome!  Very cool usage of both low key photography and black on black.  excellent job!  I''m guessing quite a bit of this was done in photoshop, but it''s just very well done.  I like your use of negative space on the left side of the photo, makes you wonder what this kid is looking at.  Once again... well done, this is the photo that first caught me eye, it''s the first one I''m voting on, so it''s definitely my first 10 :-)  Good lucK!</td>', 'The thumb looks pitch black, the photo looks fricking awesome!  Very cool usage of both low key photography and black on black.  excellent job!  I''m guessing quite a bit of this was done in photoshop, but it''s just very well done.  I like your use of negative space on the left side of the photo, makes you wonder what this kid is looking at.  Once again... well done, this is the photo that first caught me eye, it''s the first one I''m voting on, so it''s definitely my first 10 :-)  Good lucK!', '2003-06-20 04:01:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(332286, 25466, 4967, '<td valign="top">I know that this was an open editing challenge, but what you did to this photo makes it, in my mind, appear to be overprocessed, and look like a drawing/water color or something.  I''m not sure I really care for what you did here.  I think that emphasis on a photography website should still be put on the original picture more than the editing, even in an free for all editing challenge.  Just my opinion though.</td>', 'I know that this was an open editing challenge, but what you did to this photo makes it, in my mind, appear to be overprocessed, and look like a drawing/water color or something.  I''m not sure I really care for what you did here.  I think that emphasis on a photography website should still be put on the original picture more than the editing, even in an free for all editing challenge.  Just my opinion though.', '2003-06-20 04:03:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(332287, 24902, 4967, '<td valign="top">Interesting... hard to tell if this is an old man, or a mask.  I really like it.  The eyes kind of bother me, I wish I could see them more, they look so sunken and eerie.  I think in this case I would have actually liked to have seen more of the left side of the face, it is almost too black, but I guess thats the challenge.  Awesome texture here!  -8-</td>', 'Interesting... hard to tell if this is an old man, or a mask.  I really like it.  The eyes kind of bother me, I wish I could see them more, they look so sunken and eerie.  I think in this case I would have actually liked to have seen more of the left side of the face, it is almost too black, but I guess thats the challenge.  Awesome texture here!  -8-', '2003-06-20 04:05:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(332288, 25087, 4967, '<td valign="top">What a sensual photo.  The strands of hair at the side make this picture.  I really like it.  The soft feel of a not too sharp photo, which I''m guessing was intentional to go with what looks to be a kind and soft person.  Simple and nice... a well done photo.  Good luck! -9-</td>', 'What a sensual photo.  The strands of hair at the side make this picture.  I really like it.  The soft feel of a not too sharp photo, which I''m guessing was intentional to go with what looks to be a kind and soft person.  Simple and nice... a well done photo.  Good luck! -9-', '2003-06-20 04:09:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(332289, 25520, 4967, '<td valign="top">This is totally awesome and very well done.  The photo (I assume it''s one and then flippled?) is wonderfully done in the lowkey fashion, and the border just adds to it.  Very nice job here!  I''m giving it my second -10- of the challenge</td>', 'This is totally awesome and very well done.  The photo (I assume it''s one and then flippled?) is wonderfully done in the lowkey fashion, and the border just adds to it.  Very nice job here!  I''m giving it my second -10- of the challenge', '2003-06-20 04:13:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(332290, 25436, 4967, '<td valign="top">A DrJones portrait?  This is wonderful, the black (latex?) is so form fitting, you can see the every movement, against the grey background, which technically is a shade of black it''s very well done.  the lighting, everything is well done here.  If that is indeed a real person, which I assume it is, how does she breath?  -10-</td>', 'A DrJones portrait?  This is wonderful, the black (latex?) is so form fitting, you can see the every movement, against the grey background, which technically is a shade of black it''s very well done.  the lighting, everything is well done here.  If that is indeed a real person, which I assume it is, how does she breath?  -10-', '2003-06-20 04:16:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(332292, 25471, 4967, '<td valign="top">LOL... oh gees... nice job.  very interesting and intriguing.  why did you choose to leave out the head?  I like what you did with the border inside of the all editing allowed area, because it doesn''t really change the photo, just enhances it.  This isn''t a perfect photo, but I''m going out on a limb and giving it a -10- good luck!</td>', 'LOL... oh gees... nice job.  very interesting and intriguing.  why did you choose to leave out the head?  I like what you did with the border inside of the all editing allowed area, because it doesn''t really change the photo, just enhances it.  This isn''t a perfect photo, but I''m going out on a limb and giving it a -10- good luck!', '2003-06-20 04:19:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(332295, 25465, 6388, '<td valign="top">humour is good.  especially in such a dark challenge.  nice shot.</td>', 'humour is good.  especially in such a dark challenge.  nice shot.', '2003-06-20 04:21:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(332296, 25260, 4967, '<td valign="top">I pushed the arrow key as much as possible on this one, I wanted to delay commenting on it, because it''s a hard photo to deal with.  Questions run through my mind... is this a cry for help?  a cry for pity?  or a bold statement against the norm?  what is the artist trying to achieve here?  Is this the artist doing the cutting of their own body?  is it a friend (doubtful but could be) why does one cut themselves... I''m sure you''ve had a lot of people voting on this challenge totally skip by this photo, they give it their rating and continue on without blinking their eyes... I can''t do that... I kept coming back to this photo, knowing I wanted to say something, but not knowing what to say.  I guess I still don''t know what to say... this is one of the most thought provoking photos I''ve come across at DPC, and as a piece of art that is quite an achievement.  I guess you realize the horificness of this, as you have put it in a somewhat onimous, dark challenge.  I only hope that in time, the person in the photo, or you, will come to realize that life is not all that bad that you need to make yourself hurt.  I do not like the subject of this photo, I do not think it is a tremendously done well crafted photo.  I do think that it made me think and in that regard I have no choice but to give it a 10.  If you need to talk at any time, feel free to contact me.</td>', 'I pushed the arrow key as much as possible on this one, I wanted to delay commenting on it, because it''s a hard photo to deal with.  Questions run through my mind... is this a cry for help?  a cry for pity?  or a bold statement against the norm?  what is the artist trying to achieve here?  Is this the artist doing the cutting of their own body?  is it a friend (doubtful but could be) why does one cut themselves... I''m sure you''ve had a lot of people voting on this challenge totally skip by this photo, they give it their rating and continue on without blinking their eyes... I can''t do that... I kept coming back to this photo, knowing I wanted to say something, but not knowing what to say.  I guess I still don''t know what to say... this is one of the most thought provoking photos I''ve come across at DPC, and as a piece of art that is quite an achievement.  I guess you realize the horificness of this, as you have put it in a somewhat onimous, dark challenge.  I only hope that in time, the person in the photo, or you, will come to realize that life is not all that bad that you need to make yourself hurt.  I do not like the subject of this photo, I do not think it is a tremendously done well crafted photo.  I do think that it made me think and in that regard I have no choice but to give it a 10.  If you need to talk at any time, feel free to contact me.', '2003-06-20 04:26:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(332300, 25436, 8760, '<td valign="top">Woaw....Impressive photo !! Don''t know how she can breathe, but I hope for her that she didn''t has to pose for a long time !. To quality, fits perfectly my idea of a "Black on Black" picture !</td>', 'Woaw....Impressive photo !! Don''t know how she can breathe, but I hope for her that she didn''t has to pose for a long time !. To quality, fits perfectly my idea of a "Black on Black" picture !', '2003-06-20 04:31:49.000000', NULL, 1),
