(340381, 25368, 1202, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Critique<br/> <br/>Name of Photograph:  Profile in Low Key, by OneSweetSin<br/> <br/>Composition: This picture is composed very well, you have good balance here and a wondefully different perspective of the subject.   The elements of this picture lend themselves to the low key challenge very well.<br/> <br/>Technical Aspects: Your lighting is wonderful, I especially like the blending of the black background with his hair and outline of his form.   The skin tone is left quite flat which is the biggest problem with the shot,  this factor has left out most of the detail and texture of his skin and natural details around his eye and mouth.<br/> <br/>Challenge: I feel, with my limited knowledge, that this picture fits low key much better that many of those that scored higher.   <br/> <br/>Suggestions:  My only suggestion is try to get more detail to show off his young skin tones and facial features.   If it were mine I would make a quality print and hang it where every one would see it.   Good job.<br/> <br/>Disclaimer: <br/>Bear in mind that I am here to learn, just as many others and any comments that I have made are not intended to be offensive in any way, and are only constructive criticisms. If you wish to comment or discuss this critique please feel free to do so at any time. <br/>Thank you, <br/>Dick Pattee (Autool) <br/>Autool@attbi.com <br/> <br/></td>', 'Critique Club Critique Name of Photograph:  Profile in Low Key, by OneSweetSin Composition: This picture is composed very well, you have good balance here and a wondefully different perspective of the subject.   The elements of this picture lend themselves to the low key challenge very well. Technical Aspects: Your lighting is wonderful, I especially like the blending of the black background with his hair and outline of his form.   The skin tone is left quite flat which is the biggest problem with the shot,  this factor has left out most of the detail and texture of his skin and natural details around his eye and mouth. Challenge: I feel, with my limited knowledge, that this picture fits low key much better that many of those that scored higher.    Suggestions:  My only suggestion is try to get more detail to show off his young skin tones and facial features.   If it were mine I would make a quality print and hang it where every one would see it.   Good job. Disclaimer: Bear in mind that I am here to learn, just as many others and any comments that I have made are not intended to be offensive in any way, and are only constructive criticisms. If you wish to comment or discuss this critique please feel free to do so at any time. Thank you, Dick Pattee (Autool) Autool@attbi.com  ', '2003-06-27 12:11:32.000000', NULL, 0),
