(340894, 25565, 6458, '<td valign="top">There''s a reason you''re tops in my statistically favorite photographer list and this is it. I gave this a pure and unreserved 10 - you make the ivy look dangerous and alive. Good job.</td>', 'There''s a reason you''re tops in my statistically favorite photographer list and this is it. I gave this a pure and unreserved 10 - you make the ivy look dangerous and alive. Good job.', '2003-06-27 20:27:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(340975, 25070, 3080, '<td valign="top">*Critique Club*<br/>This is a very nice low key shot.  Not what I had envisioned "black on black" to be, but I definately see how it could be considered that way.  Since I''m not voting though, who cares what I think. lol<br/>I think that the lighting is wonderful.  Really nicely lit on the egg and egg cup.  I like how it only shows a slight bit of the subject and leaves the rest to our imagination.<br/>The negative space is great.  I dont think there is too much at all.  I think that the negative space is what really makes this visually appealing to me.  The lighting is awesome, but I don''t think it would have the same punch if it were centered in the frame.<br/>Focus and clarity look to be good, it''s hard to tellm but seems just fine to me. Had it been blurry looking, I think it would be obvious and non appealing.<br/>Overall a really nice job.  Definately a good shot, and I don''t really have any suggestions on improvement, as the whole shot appeals to me.<br/>Great shooting!<br/>~Heather~</td>', '*Critique Club*This is a very nice low key shot.  Not what I had envisioned "black on black" to be, but I definately see how it could be considered that way.  Since I''m not voting though, who cares what I think. lolI think that the lighting is wonderful.  Really nicely lit on the egg and egg cup.  I like how it only shows a slight bit of the subject and leaves the rest to our imagination.The negative space is great.  I dont think there is too much at all.  I think that the negative space is what really makes this visually appealing to me.  The lighting is awesome, but I don''t think it would have the same punch if it were centered in the frame.Focus and clarity look to be good, it''s hard to tellm but seems just fine to me. Had it been blurry looking, I think it would be obvious and non appealing.Overall a really nice job.  Definately a good shot, and I don''t really have any suggestions on improvement, as the whole shot appeals to me.Great shooting!~Heather~', '2003-06-27 21:56:50.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(341092, 25565, 4493, '<td valign="top">Excellent pic Indi, one of my 10''s! Great job in being 5th!</td>', 'Excellent pic Indi, one of my 10''s! Great job in being 5th!', '2003-06-28 01:12:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(341116, 25440, 8911, '<td valign="top">I loved this one - ghostly and beautiful - it shows fine on my laptop, dim but very clear.</td>', 'I loved this one - ghostly and beautiful - it shows fine on my laptop, dim but very clear.', '2003-06-28 01:42:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(341153, 25514, 6202, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>This is definately one abstract, still trying to decide if it is black  licorice or one of those recycled tire welcome mats.  But I will go with licorice.   <br/> <br/>Your dof and focus seem very good here and there is a really wonderful texture, its the glare or points of highlight here that I don''t like, they are just slightly too strong and make it appear to be more of just a macro of black licorice than a low key photo.<br/> <br/>This was definately one of the orginal photos in this challenge and definately nicely done.<br/> <br/>Anna</td>', 'Critique Club This is definately one abstract, still trying to decide if it is black  licorice or one of those recycled tire welcome mats.  But I will go with licorice.    Your dof and focus seem very good here and there is a really wonderful texture, its the glare or points of highlight here that I don''t like, they are just slightly too strong and make it appear to be more of just a macro of black licorice than a low key photo. This was definately one of the orginal photos in this challenge and definately nicely done. Anna', '2003-06-28 01:58:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(341284, 24730, 6771, '<td valign="top">I think this is a well done shot for this challenge.  Maybe a touch more light, also, from another angle to bring out the watch band a touch and maybe able to see the watch numbers a touch more.  Good focus, but kinda flat  6<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-06-28 10:17:18.</i></td>', 'I think this is a well done shot for this challenge.  Maybe a touch more light, also, from another angle to bring out the watch band a touch and maybe able to see the watch numbers a touch more.  Good focus, but kinda flat  6', '2003-06-28 11:16:35.000000', '2003-06-28 11:17:18.000000', 0),
(341302, 25565, 1143, '<td valign="top">Thanks!<br/>This is a good example of photoshop really helping a mediocre shot.<br/>It wouldn''t normally be legal b/c I did a layer with gaussian blur and soft light to give the soft focus and really bring out the highlights. I also used dodge/burn some, but the highlights on the leaves were caused by the light coming in under the bridge from the right. Exposure compensation -1/3.<br/>These are next to a train yard downtown. I didn''t have much choice in composition because they''re leaning against a bridge support... chainlink fence with a distracting background to the right and left.</td>', 'Thanks!This is a good example of photoshop really helping a mediocre shot.It wouldn''t normally be legal b/c I did a layer with gaussian blur and soft light to give the soft focus and really bring out the highlights. I also used dodge/burn some, but the highlights on the leaves were caused by the light coming in under the bridge from the right. Exposure compensation -1/3.These are next to a train yard downtown. I didn''t have much choice in composition because they''re leaning against a bridge support... chainlink fence with a distracting background to the right and left.', '2003-06-28 12:37:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(341310, 25259, 6900, '<td valign="top">You faker!  You faking butterfly nature faker!  How dareth thou post such a crock of butterfly faking manure.<br/> <br/>Ok, for real now:<br/> <br/>I gave this shot a 6.  I think it''s got nice lighting, but not that dramatic or exciting and the subject seemed more like "color" than "black" - the things I would notice anyways.<br/> <br/>No 1s is good, no 10s either - you did a technically sound shot that just didn''t irritate, annoy, grab, excite or energize.<br/> <br/>And TWO comments?  Eesh.<br/> <br/>Now 3. :)<br/> <br/>M</td>', 'You faker!  You faking butterfly nature faker!  How dareth thou post such a crock of butterfly faking manure. Ok, for real now: I gave this shot a 6.  I think it''s got nice lighting, but not that dramatic or exciting and the subject seemed more like "color" than "black" - the things I would notice anyways. No 1s is good, no 10s either - you did a technically sound shot that just didn''t irritate, annoy, grab, excite or energize. And TWO comments?  Eesh. Now 3. :) M', '2003-06-28 13:18:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(341667, 25126, 9668, '<td valign="top">Totally on, that is so it. Believe in him for eternal life. oh, and nice photograph</td>', 'Totally on, that is so it. Believe in him for eternal life. oh, and nice photograph', '2003-06-29 05:26:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(341716, 24878, 9711, '<td valign="top">when all has been said and done, the only thing to do is to live more lively not showing that you have failed and wait for tommorrow to happen!<br/>i love this photo, specially the story that can be beneath the black and white photo. it''s not just a pic but a story that is not told! and the light gives it a great character!</td>', 'when all has been said and done, the only thing to do is to live more lively not showing that you have failed and wait for tommorrow to happen!i love this photo, specially the story that can be beneath the black and white photo. it''s not just a pic but a story that is not told! and the light gives it a great character!', '2003-06-29 10:24:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(341919, 24749, 5112, '<td valign="top">FROM THE CRITIQUE CLUB<br/> <br/>Hello, Matt,<br/> <br/>I get another of your pictures to critique.  That''s OK, I like your pictures (although I''m not sure about the graphs you''ve been posting - they, the graphs, lack a certain emotional appeal :)  Anyway.  I''m trying to be "funny" and (as my kids would say), "You''re not good at that, mum."<br/> <br/>About "Seeing visions":<br/> <br/>First impressions: it''s a good entry to black on black.  It looks spooky.  I liked it a lot during the challenge, but I had just a little trouble putting the picture and the title together.  I mean, I can see the "vision", or, the pict looks like a vision, but during the challenge I remember thinking, "who is seeing visions?".<br/> <br/>Technical:  No problems.  Lighting, focus, everything looks fine, or at least as I imagine you intended it to look.  I like the post-processing, very nice.  I really like the texture/colours of the cross, it looks rounded, and very stone-like.  The cross is my favourite part of the picture.<br/> <br/>Composition:  Also no problems, except for what I mentioned above about the title.  I like the placement of the objects, and all the black around them.  I think no border is a good choice in this case.<br/> <br/>Overall:  Good shot.  So, why didn''t it do better?  I don''t know.  This was a very confusing challenge, rather misunderstood (or not understood).  I think it was very difficult to pick winners, and this picture, even though good, probably didn''t hold the viewer''s attention long enough.  It takes a moment to figure it out.  I think what I''m trying to say is that this shot is maybe a bit too subtle for its intention?  I''m not sure.<br/> <br/>Anyway.  Keep going!  By the way, what is Theoretical Ecology, and how is it different from studying just straight Ecology?  <br/> <br/>Take care,<br/> <br/>Ursula (uabresch)<br/></td>', 'FROM THE CRITIQUE CLUB Hello, Matt, I get another of your pictures to critique.  That''s OK, I like your pictures (although I''m not sure about the graphs you''ve been posting - they, the graphs, lack a certain emotional appeal :)  Anyway.  I''m trying to be "funny" and (as my kids would say), "You''re not good at that, mum." About "Seeing visions": First impressions: it''s a good entry to black on black.  It looks spooky.  I liked it a lot during the challenge, but I had just a little trouble putting the picture and the title together.  I mean, I can see the "vision", or, the pict looks like a vision, but during the challenge I remember thinking, "who is seeing visions?". Technical:  No problems.  Lighting, focus, everything looks fine, or at least as I imagine you intended it to look.  I like the post-processing, very nice.  I really like the texture/colours of the cross, it looks rounded, and very stone-like.  The cross is my favourite part of the picture. Composition:  Also no problems, except for what I mentioned above about the title.  I like the placement of the objects, and all the black around them.  I think no border is a good choice in this case. Overall:  Good shot.  So, why didn''t it do better?  I don''t know.  This was a very confusing challenge, rather misunderstood (or not understood).  I think it was very difficult to pick winners, and this picture, even though good, probably didn''t hold the viewer''s attention long enough.  It takes a moment to figure it out.  I think what I''m trying to say is that this shot is maybe a bit too subtle for its intention?  I''m not sure. Anyway.  Keep going!  By the way, what is Theoretical Ecology, and how is it different from studying just straight Ecology?   Take care, Ursula (uabresch)', '2003-06-29 19:43:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(341952, 24946, 2130, '<td valign="top">I think this photo is just too small for a print...I don´t own a larger copy :(  but thanx 2u all for your uplifting comments :)</td>', 'I think this photo is just too small for a print...I don´t own a larger copy :(  but thanx 2u all for your uplifting comments :)', '2003-06-29 21:47:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(343878, 25174, 8127, '<td valign="top">Hi, really love this pic, the composition &amp; lighting are great! :o) Well done &amp; well deserved win :o)</td>', 'Hi, really love this pic, the composition & lighting are great! :o) Well done & well deserved win :o)', '2003-07-01 19:33:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(344033, 24946, 5940, '<td valign="top">the border could have been more helpful to the picture if you would''ve made all the leaves overlap it rather than overlap only at the bottom. My favorite part of your picture is the very bottom where the leaves have a glowing white around them and the texture is the strongest, also the leaves appear to be coming at you since the border gets lost around the tip.<br/></td>', 'the border could have been more helpful to the picture if you would''ve made all the leaves overlap it rather than overlap only at the bottom. My favorite part of your picture is the very bottom where the leaves have a glowing white around them and the texture is the strongest, also the leaves appear to be coming at you since the border gets lost around the tip.', '2003-07-02 00:13:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(344038, 25480, 5940, '<td valign="top">It''s a nice subject but the postioning could be better and with an added something to the background it would work great</td>', 'It''s a nice subject but the postioning could be better and with an added something to the background it would work great', '2003-07-02 00:17:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(344042, 24766, 5940, '<td valign="top">nice photo but it has a lot of distractions that take away from the great quality</td>', 'nice photo but it has a lot of distractions that take away from the great quality', '2003-07-02 00:19:58.000000', NULL, 0),
